# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# credmgr — deny-by-default secret hygiene
#
# This file is the SECOND line of defence, not the first. The first is that the
# vault does not live here at all: lib/paths.js resolves it to the platform's
# user-data directory (~/Library/Application Support/credmgr, %APPDATA%\credmgr,
# ~/.local/share/credmgr). A path outside the repository is a guarantee; a
# .gitignore is only a promise.
#
# The third line is scripts/guard-no-secrets.mjs, installed as a pre-commit
# hook by `npm run hooks:install` and run in CI. It blocks the commit.
#
# If you are adding a new file type that could ever hold a secret, add it here
# FIRST and commit that change on its own.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── The vault itself (belt and braces — it should never be in-tree) ─────────
.credmgr/
store/
backups/
archive/
*.age
*.tar.age
vault.sha256

# ── Key material, any shape, anywhere ──────────────────────────────────────
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
*.kubeconfig
*.asc
*.gpg
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*_rsa
*_ecdsa
*_ed25519
!*.pub.example

# ── Environment files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

# ── Cloud / service credential files ───────────────────────────────────────
credentials.json
service-account*.json
gcp-key*.json
firebase-adminsdk-*.json
aws-credentials*
.npmrc
.netrc
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.toml
*.mobileprovision

# ── Wallet / chain material ────────────────────────────────────────────────
*mnemonic*
*seed-phrase*
*seedphrase*
keystore/
wallets.json
**/receive-addresses-*.json

# ── Plaintext credential dumps people accidentally create ──────────────────
*credential*.txt
*credentials*.md
*password*.txt
*secret*.txt
*token*.txt
*.local
*.rtf

# ── Build / tooling / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ── Local agent / editor state (not secrets, just not for git) ─────────────
.codemap/
.remember/
.planning/
.cleanup_state/

# ── Local agent context, not product documentation ─────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md describes the maintainer's local three-location layout (live vault /
# public source / V2 design) and their machine's paths. Useful to an agent working
# here; meaningless and mildly revealing to anyone else. It stays on disk and out
# of the repository.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
